invariant: INV-14
file: srv.c
catches: proof/prove-one.sh srv_accept
reason: a server with no ticket_key takes a cookie_key of all zero bytes,
  so anyone mints the cookies of its HelloRetryRequest. The srv_accept
  harness gives each key zeros and one byte of any value, and requires
  that the flight runs only under keys that meet srv_cfg.h's rules.

--- old
static int keys_ok(const ch_srv_cfg *srv) {
--- new
static int keys_ok(const ch_srv_cfg *srv) {
    if (srv->ticket_key == NULL) {
        return srv->cookie_key != NULL;
    }
